From: Nura local rear-camera port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: enable the guacamole rear flash as a bring-up torch

The 7.0 board delta describes the PM8150L flash block only through
pm8150l.dtsi: SPMI slave 5 exists and is enabled, but its
led-controller@d300 child is "disabled" and has no LED children, so
leds-qcom-flash never binds and there is no /sys/class/leds/*:torch.

Enable it as a torch only. One ganged LED on flash channels 1 and 2:
the binding and driver split a ganged LED's current symmetrically over
its channels and switch them together, and Plasma Mobile's flashlight
quick setting handles one LED.

led-max-microamp is deliberately the conservative bring-up value, not
the stock 300 mA per channel. The only current setting verified on this
hardware was the reference's 32/255 on a 300 mA-max single-channel LED
for 2 s. The driver's integer scaling turns that into a 37 mA request
and ITARGET 6, i.e. 35 mA per channel at 5 mA torch resolution (70 mA
for both LEDs). A 70000 uA ganged node at full brightness requests
35 mA per channel and writes the same ITARGET 6, so Plasma's
max_brightness write lands exactly on the verified setting.

flash-max-microamp/flash-max-timeout-us are omitted on purpose: the LED
advertises no strobe capability until the stock 1 A per channel flash
current has its own validation. The stock production node (300 mA per
channel torch, 1 A per channel flash, 1.28 s) is a separate follow-up
patch.

Nura-Category: device-dt
Nura-Origin: nura local
Upstream-Status: n/a: guacamole DTS is not upstream

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <dt-bindings/input/linux-event-codes.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6asm.h>
 
 / {
@@ -555,3 +556,31 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Rear dual LED flash on PM8150L (SPMI slave 5), on flash channels 1 and 2.
+ *
+ * Bring-up stage: torch only, one ganged LED, and a cap that reproduces the
+ * one current setting that was actually verified on this hardware. The
+ * reference test drove each LED alone as its own 300 mA-max classdev at
+ * brightness 32/255 for 2 s. The driver's integer scaling turns that into a
+ * 37 mA request, ITARGET 6, i.e. 35 mA per channel (5 mA torch resolution),
+ * 70 mA for both LEDs. At full brightness a 70000 uA ganged node requests
+ * 35 mA per channel and writes the same ITARGET 6, so Plasma Mobile's
+ * max_brightness toggle lands exactly on the verified condition.
+ *
+ * No flash-max-microamp/flash-max-timeout-us here: the LED exposes no strobe
+ * capability until the stock flash currents have their own validation.
+ * Stock values (300 mA/channel torch, 1 A/channel flash, 1.28 s) and the
+ * production node are a separate follow-up patch.
+ */
+&pm8150l_flash {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	led-0 {
+		function = LED_FUNCTION_TORCH;
+		color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+		led-sources = <1 2>;
+		led-max-microamp = <70000>;
+	};
+};
